---
import GuideLinks from './GuideLinks.astro';
---
<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14">
  <h2 class="text-2xl mb-8">Coming from KlipperScreen or a factory screen</h2>
  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-x-10 gap-y-10">
    <article>
      <h3 class="text-lg mb-2">If you run KlipperScreen</h3>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted mb-3">
        HelixScreen has screens for Happy Hare and AFC, so an ERCF or Box Turtle shows its
        filament path, the spool in each slot and buffer health on the touchscreen. Each
        spool's remaining weight is tracked as it prints.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted mb-3">
        It needs about 15 MB of RAM against <a href="https://github.com/KlipperScreen/KlipperScreen" class="text-secondary underline underline-offset-2">KlipperScreen</a>'s 50, and no X11 or Wayland. The
        home screen is a grid of widgets you arrange, in any of 18 themes.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted mb-3">
        KlipperScreen has 32 translations to HelixScreen's 10, so check your language first.
      </p>
      <GuideLinks links={[
        { href: '/guide/filament-ams-panel/', label: 'Multi-Filament Panel' },
        { href: '/guide/settings/appearance/#built-in-themes', label: 'Built-in Themes' },
        { href: '/guide/settings/language-time/#language', label: 'Language' },
      ]} />
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3 class="text-lg mb-2">If your printer has a factory screen</h3>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted mb-3">
        HelixScreen runs the multi-material units those printers ship with: <a href="/guide/filament-cfs/" class="text-secondary underline underline-offset-2">Creality CFS</a>, the
        AD5X's IFS and Anycubic ACE. It also works with Spoolman.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted mb-3">
        Klipper and Moonraker stay as they are. Only the screen changes.
      </p>
      <GuideLinks links={[
        { href: '/guide/supported-printers/#deeply-integrated-printers', label: 'Deeply Integrated Printers' },
        { href: '/guide/filament-tracking/#tracking-with-spoolman', label: 'Tracking With Spoolman' },
      ]} />
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3 class="text-lg mb-2">Installing it, and going back</h3>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted mb-3">
        One command installs it and stops KlipperScreen for you. On first launch it detects
        the printer and its hardware, so there is little to configure.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted mb-3">
        <code class="font-mono text-xs text-ink">--uninstall</code> puts back the screen you
        had before, stock or KlipperScreen. <a href="/installation/" class="text-secondary underline underline-offset-2">The install guide</a> has the details for each printer.
      </p>
      <GuideLinks links={[
        { href: '/guide/getting-started/#first-time-setup', label: 'First-Time Setup' },
        { href: '/installation/#uninstalling', label: 'Uninstalling' },
      ]} />
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
